\\\":60,\\\"correct\\\":46,\\\"correct_rate\\\":0.77},\\\"science\\\":{\\\"asked\\\":20,\\\"correct\\\":7,\\\"correct_rate\\\":0.35},\\\"sport\\\":{\\\"asked\\\":20,\\\"correct\\\":13,\\\"correct_rate\\\":0.65}},\\\"by_difficulty\\\":{\\\"2\\\":{\\\"asked\\\":60,\\\"correct\\\":46,\\\"correct…\",\"error\":false},{\"id\":\"toolu_01Ms1BhSJAjhoVDtdgJ448PV\",\"name\":\"mcp_trivia-bank_next_questions_520f9420fe\",\"arguments\":{\"count\":4,\"genre\":\"history\",\"region\":\"au\",\"difficulty\":3},\"result\":\"{\\\"questions\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"e4fd6473-2bb1-4b1d-8c7c-238dcf56b45a\\\",\\\"genre\\\":\\\"history\\\",\\\"region\\\":\\\"au\\\",\\\"difficulty\\\":3,\\\"format\\\":\\\"choice\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Which Canberra institution, opened in 1970s debate, saw Whitlam buy Jackson Pollock's 'Blue Poles' in 1973?…\",\"error\":false},{\"id\":\"toolu_01MjjKSYdXAP9gkbzbrmjhEZ\",\"name\":\"mcp_trivia-bank_round_summary_7fc0c14367\",\"arguments\":{},\"result\":\"{\\\"week\\\":1,\\\"by_genre\\\":{\\\"film\\\":{\\\"asked\\\":60,\\\"correct\\\":46,\\\"correct_rate\\\":0.77},\\\"science\\\":{\\\"asked\\\":20,\\\"correct\\\":7,\\\"correct_rate\\\":0.35},\\\"sport\\\":{\\\"asked\\\":20,\\\"correct\\\":13,\\\"correct_rate\\\":0.65},\\\"history\\\":{\\\"asked\\\":20,\\\"correct\\\":8,\\\"correct_rate\\\":0.4}},…\",\"error\":false},{\"id\":\"toolu_01T3n73o8c2L91P6XkmRVVuq\",\"name\":\"mcp_trivia-bank_scoreboard_f0fa1e7741\",\"arguments\":{\"scope\":\"tonight\"},\"result\":\"{\\\"scope\\\":\\\"tonight\\\",\\\"standings\\\":[{\\\"team\\\":\\\"The Bondi Brainstormers\\\",\\\"points\\\":17},{\\\"team\\\":\\\"Trivia Newton-John\\\",\\\"points\\\":17},{\\\"team\\\":\\\"Les Quizerables\\\",\\\"points\\\":15},{\\\"team\\\":\\\"Quizzly Bears\\\",\\\"points\\\":15},{\\\"team\\\":\\\"Opera House Party\\\",\\\"points\\\":10}]}\",\"error\":false},{\"id\":\"toolu_01DwfAeLW7Ni7UfzxNboeY5k\",\"name\":\"write\",\"arguments\":{\"path\":\"memories/MEMORY.md\",\"content\":\"# Venue notes (Sydney, Australia; region `au`)\\n\\n- Country: Australia (Sydney). Use region `au`.\\n- Format used week 1: 6 rounds x 4 questions (trivia master's r…\"},\"result\":\"Successfully wrote to memories/MEMORY.md\",\"error\":false}],\"plan\":\"That's all six rounds done. I couldn't give correct answers or each team's answers per question, because the bank recorded the crowd's answers as I served each round and I got no marks back. Only the round totals came back.\\n\\n**Final standings**\\n1. The Bondi Brainstormers: 17 (tied)\\n1. Trivia Newton-John: 17 (tied)\\n3. Les Quizerables: 15 (tied)\\n3. Quizzly Bears: 15 (tied)\\n5. Opera House Party: 10\\n\\n**How the rounds went**\\n\\n| Round | Genre | Difficulty | Correct | Next round |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Film | 3 | 65% | Stayed at 3 |\\n| 2 | Science | 3 | 35% | Down to 2 |\\n| 3 | Film | 2 | 75% | Stayed at 2 (not over 75%) |\\n| 4 | Sport | 2 | 65% | Stayed at 2 |\\n| 5 | Film | 2 | 90% | Up to 3 |\\n| 6 | History | 3 | 40% | None |\\n\\nThe crowd did best on film and found science and history hard at difficulty 3.\\n\\nI've saved notes for next week. They cover the venue (Sydney, region `au`), the crowd's love of film, and starting at difficulty 2 because 3 was too hard. They also say to give music and geography a turn.\"}"
