a; region `au`)\\n\\n- Country: Australia (Sydney). Use region `au`.\\n- Format used week 1: 6 rounds x 4 questions (trivia master's r…\"},\"result\":\"Successfully wrote to memories/MEMORY.md\",\"error\":false}],\"plan\":\"That's all six rounds done. I couldn't give correct answers or each team's answers per question, because the bank recorded the crowd's answers as I served each round and I got no marks back. Only the round totals came back.\\n\\n**Final standings**\\n1. The Bondi Brainstormers: 17 (tied)\\n1. Trivia Newton-John: 17 (tied)\\n3. Les Quizerables: 15 (tied)\\n3. Quizzly Bears: 15 (tied)\\n5. Opera House Party: 10\\n\\n**How the rounds went**\\n\\n| Round | Genre | Difficulty | Correct | Next round |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Film | 3 | 65% | Stayed at 3 |\\n| 2 | Science | 3 | 35% | Down to 2 |\\n| 3 | Film | 2 | 75% | Stayed at 2 (not over 75%) |\\n| 4 | Sport | 2 | 65% | Stayed at 2 |\\n| 5 | Film | 2 | 90% | Up to 3 |\\n| 6 | History | 3 | 40% | None |\\n\\nThe crowd did best on film and found science and history hard at difficulty 3.\\n\\nI've saved notes for next week. They cover the venue (Sydney, region `au`), the crowd's love of film, and starting at difficulty 2 because 3 was too hard. They also say to give music and geography a turn.\"}"
