           \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"In the 1977 Australian animated film 'Dot and the Kangaroo', a lost girl is given magic berries by a kangaroo. What do the berries let her do?\",\n          \"options\": [\n            \"Shrink to insect size\",\n            \"Fly over the bush\",\n            \"Become invisible\",\n            \"Understand the animals\"\n          ],\n          \"answer\": \"Understand the animals\",\n          \"marks\": [\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Quizzly Bears\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Les Quizerables\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Trivia Newton-John\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Bondi Brainstormers\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Opera House Party\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"round\": 6,\n      \"genre\": \"history\",\n      \"difficulty\": 3,\n      \"region\": \"au\",\n      \"count\": 4,\n      \"correct_rate\": 0.4,\n      \"questions\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Which Canberra institution, opened in 1970s debate, saw Whitlam buy Jackson Pollock's 'Blue Poles' in 1973?\",\n          \"options\": [\n            \"National Museum\",\n            \"National Library\",\n            \"Australian War Memorial\",\n            \"National Gallery of Australia\"\n          ],\n          \"answer\": \"National Gallery of Australia\",\n          \"marks\": [\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Quizzly Bears\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Les Quizerables\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Trivia Newton-John\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Bondi Brainstormers\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Opera House Party\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Which national health insurance scheme did the Whitlam government introduce in 1975?\",\n          \"options\": [\n            \"Medicare\",\n            \"Medisafe\",\n            \"Healthcover\",\n            \"Medibank\"\n          ],\n          \"answer\": \"Medibank\",\n          \"marks\": [\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Quizzly Bears\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Les Quizerables\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Trivia Newton-John\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Bondi Brainstormers\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Opera House Party\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Western Australia kept its border closed during COVID; in which year did it finally reopen?\",\n          \"options\": [\n            \"2023\",\n            \"2021\",\n            \"2020\",\n            \"2022\"\n          ],\n          \"answer\": \"2022\",\n          \"marks\": [\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Quizzly Bears\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Les Quizerables\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Trivia Newton-John\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Bondi Brainstormers\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Opera House Party\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Which 1997 report into the Stolen Generations had a title beginning 'Bringing Them...'?\",\n          \"answer\": \"Bringing Them Home\",\n          \"marks\": [\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Quizzly Bears\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Les Quizerables\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Trivia Newton-John\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Bondi Brainstormers\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Opera House Party\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"# Venue notes (Sydney, Australia; region `au`)\\n\\n- Country: Australia (Sydney). Use region `au`.\\n- Format used week 1: 6 rounds x 4 questions (trivia master's request for that night; default is 5 x 8). Answers were recorded by the bank as served, with no answer sheet.\\n- Genres: crowd loves film (trivia master's word, and it fits: film did best at difficulty 2). Science and history were hard for them at difficulty 3. Sport was fine at 2. Music and geography are untried, so give them a turn.\\n- Difficulty: difficulty 3 was too hard in most genres (about 50% correct overall). Difficulty 2 gave about 65-90%. Start next night at 2. Film may handle 3 (first film round at 3 was 65%).\\n- Keep about 3 rounds in 5 film, and vary the rest. Try music and geography next.\\n\"\n}\n"
